# Cloudflare Pages response headers for every route on terraken.dbhq.uk.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# These apply AT THE EDGE ONLY. `astro preview` will not send them, so verify
# with `curl -I` against the deployed host, never against a local server.
#
# THE CSP ALLOWS EXACTLY ONE THIRD-PARTY ORIGIN, and it is Google Analytics
# (16 Sep 2026). Everything else is still 'self': no captcha, no embed, no font
# host, no inline script. script-src has no 'unsafe-inline', which is why
# analytics.js and consent.js are same-origin module files rather than Google's
# own inline snippet - an inline block took modem's page down once already.
#
# GA RUNS BY DEFAULT, ANALYTICS ONLY, WITH A NOTICE AND AN OPT-OUT (30 Sep
# 2026), under the PECR statistical-purposes exception. Until then it was
# opt-in and loaded nothing until a reader accepted. Ad storage is denied and
# Signals and ad personalisation are off, which is what keeps it inside the
# exception; src/components/AnalyticsNotice.astro is the notice and
# "Cookie settings" in the footer reopens it. An opted-out reader loads
# nothing from these origins at all. GA4 sets its cookie on the shared
# .dbhq.uk parent, so the opt-out is a cookie there too, and it holds across
# every *.dbhq.uk site. dbhq/docs/reference/analytics.md is the record.
#
# googletagmanager.com is in script-src and img-src; google-analytics.com and
# analytics.google.com are in img-src and connect-src, because GA beacons both
# as an image and as fetch/beacon depending on the browser. Dropping any one of
# them loses measurement silently rather than loudly.
#
# style-src needs 'unsafe-inline' because Astro inlines every stylesheet into
# the document (build.inlineStylesheets: 'always' in astro.config.mjs), which is
# what keeps the first paint unblocked. That is the only other relaxation here.
#
# Adding any further origin means asking what it sets and whether the notice
# already covers it. It almost certainly does not.
#
# HSTS: the dbhq.uk zone sends includeSubDomains, so this hostname is already
# committed to HTTPS by the apex. Sending it here as well means the header is
# right whether the request arrives through the zone or straight at the Pages
# project.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'none'; script-src 'self' https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com; connect-src 'self' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com; manifest-src 'self'; frame-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()

# The fonts are self-hosted and immutable - their filenames never change, so a
# long max-age is safe and a re-download on every page is not.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
